<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FBType Name="Q_Attribute" Comment="Command change attribute( Part 6 - F.38 )">
	<Identification Standard="ISO 11783-6" Description="Copyright (c) 2022 HR Agrartechnik GmbH  &#10; &#10;This program and the accompanying materials are made  &#10;available under the terms of the Eclipse Public License 2.0  &#10;which is available at https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-2.0/  &#10; &#10;SPDX-License-Identifier: EPL-2.0  &#10;   &#10;   &#10;see Description Tab">
	</Identification>
	<VersionInfo Organization="HR Agrartechnik GmbH" Version="1.0" Author="Franz Höpfinger" Date="2022-07-08">
	</VersionInfo>
	<CompilerInfo packageName="isobus::UT::Q">
		<Import declaration="isobus::UT::Q::const::IDs::ID_NULL"/>
	</CompilerInfo>
	<InterfaceList>
		<EventInputs>
			<Event Name="INIT" Type="EInit" Comment="Service Initialization">
				<With Var="QI"/>
				<With Var="u16ObjId"/>
				<With Var="u8IdAttribute"/>
			</Event>
			<Event Name="REQ" Type="Event" Comment="Service Request">
				<With Var="QI"/>
				<With Var="u32ValueAttribute"/>
			</Event>
		</EventInputs>
		<EventOutputs>
			<Event Name="INITO" Type="EInit" Comment="Initialization Confirm">
				<With Var="QO"/>
			</Event>
			<Event Name="CNF" Type="Event" Comment="Confirmation of Requested Service">
				<With Var="QO"/>
				<With Var="STATUS"/>
				<With Var="u32OldValueAttribute"/>
				<With Var="s16result"/>
			</Event>
		</EventOutputs>
		<InputVars>
			<VarDeclaration Name="QI" Type="BOOL" Comment="Quality Input - TRUE to enable service" InitialValue="TRUE"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="u16ObjId" Type="UINT" Comment="Object ID " InitialValue="ID_NULL"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="u8IdAttribute" Type="USINT" Comment="Attribute ID (AID) - see description of wished object "/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="u32ValueAttribute" Type="UDINT" Comment="New value for attribute "/>
		</InputVars>
		<OutputVars>
			<VarDeclaration Name="QO" Type="BOOL" Comment="Quality Output - TRUE if service executed successfully"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="STATUS" Type="STRING" Comment="Service Status"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="u32OldValueAttribute" Type="UDINT" Comment="Old value for attribute "/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="s16result" Type="INT" Comment="retval see description"/>
		</OutputVars>
	</InterfaceList>
	<Attribute Name="Documentation" Type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<h1>Command change attribute ( Part 6 - F.38 )</h1>

<p>This command is used to change any attribute with an assigned AID. This message cannot be used to change strings. It addresses <strong>two distinct parameters</strong> with <strong>different validity rules each</strong> — <code>u16ObjId</code> (the object whose attribute is changed) and <code>u8IdAttribute</code> (the Attribute ID, AID, selecting the attribute).</p>

<h2>Valid values for u16ObjId (the object whose attribute is changed)</h2>

<p>An attribute Object ID is valid if it falls within one of the following ISO 11783-6 ID ranges (Annex F.38):</p>
<ul>
	<li><strong>DataMask</strong>: 1000 – 1999</li>
	<li><strong>AlarmMask</strong>: 2000 – 2999</li>
	<li><strong>SoftKeyMask</strong>: 4000 – 4999</li>
	<li><strong>Key</strong>: 5000 – 5999</li>
	<li><strong>Button</strong>: 6000 – 6999</li>
	<li><strong>InputBooleanField</strong>: 7000 – 7999</li>
	<li><strong>InputStringField</strong>: 8000 – 8999</li>
	<li><strong>InputNumberField</strong>: 9000 – 9999</li>
	<li><strong>InputListField</strong>: 10000 – 10999</li>
	<li><strong>AuxiliaryFunctionType2</strong>: 31000 – 31999</li>
</ul>

<h2>Valid values for u8IdAttribute (AID)</h2>

<p>The Attribute ID (AID) selects which attribute of the addressed object is changed. Valid AIDs are object-type specific and are defined in ISO 11783-6 Annex B, in the attribute table of each object type. An AID with no attribute assigned is rejected by the VT (F.39, bit 1 = Invalid Attribute ID). The new value is transmitted little endian in bytes 5–8 of the command (F.38) — this FB passes it as <code>u32ValueAttribute</code>.</p>

<p>ID_NULL (65535) is not a command target but can be used in INIT to deactivate the FB. Any ID outside these ranges is invalid for commanding.</p>

<h2>Activate / Deactivate</h2>

<p>The FB is deactivated by default. It becomes active when INIT provides a valid attribute Object ID. Sending INIT with ID_NULL (65535) deactivates the FB again. This toggle can be repeated arbitrarily.</p>

<ul>
	<li><strong>INIT + ID_NULL (65535)</strong>: FB deactivated, STATUS="DEACTIVATED", s16result=VT_E_DEACTIVATED (-40)</li>
	<li><strong>INIT + valid attribute ID</strong>: FB activated, STATUS="initialized", s16result=VT_E_NO_ERR (0). If a REQ was buffered before, it is executed immediately.</li>
	<li><strong>INIT + invalid ID</strong>: STATUS="ERROR: Invalid Object ID (not an attribute object)", s16result=VT_E_INVALID_OBJECT_ID (-132)</li>
</ul>

<h2>REQ Handling</h2>

<ul>
	<li><strong>REQ before any INIT</strong>: Buffered, STATUS="Buffered: INIT not yet completed", s16result=VT_E_NOT_READY (-131)</li>
	<li><strong>REQ while deactivated (INIT came with NULL or invalid ID)</strong>: STATUS shows the actual deactivation reason, s16result=VT_E_DEACTIVATED (-40) or VT_E_INVALID_OBJECT_ID (-132)</li>
	<li><strong>REQ while active</strong>: Command sent to VT, result reflected in CNF</li>
</ul>

<h2>param[in] {u16ObjId, uint16_t}</h2>

<p>Object ID. Use ID_NULL (65535) to deactivate the FB. Use a valid attribute object ID to activate.</p>

<h2>param[in] {u8IdAttribute, uint8_t}</h2>

<p>Attribute ID (AID) - see description of wished object</p>

<h2>param[in] {u32ValueAttribute, uint32_t}</h2>

<p>New value for attribute</p>

<h2>Return Values (s16result):</h2>

<h3>int16_t</h3>

<ul>
	<li><span style="color:#27ae60">VT_E_NO_ERR (0)</span> - OK</li>
	<li><span style="color:#f39c12">VT_E_DEACTIVATED (-40)</span> - FB deactivated (INIT received with ID_NULL)</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_INVALID_OBJECT_ID (-132)</span> - Object ID is invalid (not an attribute object)</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_NOT_READY (-131)</span> - Buffered: INIT not yet completed</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_OVERFLOW (-6)</span> - buffer overflow</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_NOACT (-8)</span> - Command not possible in current state</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_NO_INSTANCE (-21)</span> - No VT client available</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_ISO_INSTANCE_INVALID (-129)</span> - Identifier for instance (connection) invalid</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_NOT_ALIVE (-130)</span> - Identifier for instance valid, but VT Dead.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Instanz-Eindeutigkeit (Instance Uniqueness)</h2>

<p>Dieser Baustein erfordert Instanz-Eindeutigkeit bezüglich des Paares (<strong>u16ObjId</strong>, <strong>u8IdAttribute</strong>). Es darf im gesamten Programm nur eine Instanz von <code>Q_Attribute</code> für dasselbe Objekt-Attribut-Paar existieren. Eine zweite Instanz auf dieselbe Objekt-ID und Attribut-ID wird bei <code>INIT</code> deaktiviert (STATUS = "This objID is already in use").</p>
]]></Attribute>
	<Attribute Name="eclipse4diac::core::TypeHash" Value="''"/>
</FBType>
